# Gilgamesh, Master-at-Arms: "Whenever Gilgamesh enters or attacks, look at the top six cards of your library. You may put any number of Equipment
# cards from among them onto the battlefield. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in a random order. When you put one or more Equipment
# onto the battlefield this way, you may attach one of them to a Samurai you control."
# Turn 1: Bot1 casts Leonardo, Sewer Samurai. Turn 2: Bot2 casts Colleen Wing, Street Samurai, a Samurai Bot1 does not control. Turn 3: Bot1
# draws an Island and casts Gilgamesh off Black Lotus and the Moxen. The top six are Skullclamp, Grizzly Bears, Paradise Mantle, Island, Loxodon Warhammer and Island; the
# Ornithopter seventh is not looked at, and Bot2's library is not looked at at all. Neither the Bears nor the Ornithopter can be chosen;
# Skullclamp and Paradise Mantle are put onto the battlefield together and the Warhammer, an Equipment left behind, goes to the bottom. They enter
# untapped. The reflexive ability offers the two that entered, not the Warhammer, and only one of them; Skullclamp is attached to Leonardo, a Samurai Bot1 controls, chosen over
# Gilgamesh, while Bot2's Colleen Wing is not offered. Leonardo is 4/2, and Paradise Mantle stays unattached.

